hey Ron i'ma be sharp welcome to Abby's  kitchen Spring has finally sprung and  that means we are all looking for really  great fresh colorful recipes to start  our day so today I want to share with  you one of my favorite recipes from the  mindful Glo cookbook if you don't have  this book folks be sure to get it you'll  see the link below in the description  but we're going to be doing a  traditional egg base recipe because I  know Easter is coming and a lot of you  are looking for egg recipes but for my  plant-based friends and followers out  there we're gonna be making this  completely plant-based so this is my  sweet potato and black bean scramble  breakfast taco with tomatillo salsa it  is so fun it's so colorful and it's a  kind of percent vegan so you guys are  going to love it let's do that to a pan  I add a little bit of olive oil over  medium-high heat and then I add some  diced sweet potatoes and give it a good  stir until they all start to brown then  I add a can of rinsed black beans maple  syrup Chipotle and adobo sauce cumin and  cinnamon and I start to cook everything  into the sweet potato soften then I set  them aside and keep them more next to  the pan I add a little more olive oil  along with some firm tofu then I add  some turmeric and some nutritional yeast  along with a pinch of salt and I give  that a good stir and cook it until the  tofu gets nice and yellow to assemble I  layer some corn tortillas with my tofu  my sweet potato black bean mixture  some avocado some tomatillo salsa that  you're gonna need to get a copy of the  mindflow cookbook to get some crumbled  feta cheese vegan or not cilantro and  some lime enjoy  [Music]  [Music]
 

